content-briefs/bariatric-surgery-perth.md:117:Cover: total cost depends on procedure, private health cover, level of excess (out of pocket), hospital and anaesthetic fees; Medicare and private-health benefits may apply when the relevant criteria are met, but coverage and gaps vary. Any range or estimate should be discussed at consultation with an itemised breakdown. Superannuation access may be available only under specific circumstances — verify current rules. Do not quote specific dollar figures.
content-briefs/bariatric-surgery-perth.md:126:Include concise, answer-first responses to these questions: how much bariatric surgery costs in Perth (no dollar figures; any range is discussed at consultation); Medicare and private-health coverage; how to choose a procedure; sleeve versus bypass; surgical and non-surgical options; the 30/30 eating rule; who may not meet MBS or clinical suitability requirements; aftercare and what can vary over 10 years; where appointments and surgery take place (hospital identity to be verified); whether revision is possible; and how to assess a bariatric surgeon in Perth. Any GLP-1 or active-ingredient wording remains subject to the pending TGA/legal decision and must never use brand names.
content-briefs/bariatric-surgery-perth.md:131:- Medical advertising: no guarantees, use phrases like "clinical averages", "results vary", "your surgeon will advise", "many patients experience"
content-briefs/bariatric-surgery-perth.md:132:- AHPRA/TGA: no testimonials, no before/after claims, no guaranteed outcomes; weight loss percentages (e.g. 60–70% excess weight) must be framed as "many patients" or "clinical averages", never as guaranteed individual results
content-briefs/bariatric-surgery-perth.md:134:- Reader: a Perth adult who already knows what bariatric surgery is; they are comparing providers and want to trust this team with something significant; credentialism (FRACS, SJOG hospitals, 20+ years) matters here
