content-reviews/gastric-sleeve-perth.md:167:> **5. What does recovery actually look like week to week?** Your first 1-2 days post op are spent in hospital on clear fluids. Week one is rest at home, sipping carefully and managing fatigue. By weeks two to three, your diet usually progresses from fluids to pureed and soft foods. Your dietitian may advise a 30/30 approach—separating food and fluids by about 30 minutes—if this is part of your post-operative plan; follow the instructions tailored to your recovery.
content-reviews/gastric-sleeve-perth.md:169:Why it matters: This writes the missing 30/30 answer into the recovery FAQ without presenting it as a universal rule; the dietitian’s plan remains authoritative.
content-reviews/gastric-sleeve-perth.md:175:> **2. How much weight will I actually lose, and what can happen 10 years after surgery?** Average results are reported as around 60–70% of excess body weight over 12–18 months, though individual results vary. Long-term results also vary: some people maintain meaningful weight loss, while others regain some weight over the years; nutrition, reflux, medical conditions, eating patterns, activity and follow-up can all matter. Ongoing clinical review and blood tests help identify issues and guide care.
