content-briefs/gastric-sleeve-perth.md:103:3. **The procedure** — General anaesthetic, keyhole technique, 45–60 minutes. Surgeon removes ~75–80% of the stomach and seals the new sleeve with a staple line. Keep it clinical but accessible.
content-briefs/gastric-sleeve-perth.md:104:4. **Hospital recovery** — Around 2 nights at St John of God Murdoch or Subiaco. Patient starts on fluids and progresses under guidance from nursing and dietetic staff.
content-briefs/gastric-sleeve-perth.md:111:Each bullet should convey one clear, qualified benefit. Do not use superlatives.
content-briefs/gastric-sleeve-perth.md:113:1. Weight loss — clinical averages of 60–70% of excess weight over 12–18 months are reported in some studies; individual results vary and no result is guaranteed.
content-briefs/gastric-sleeve-perth.md:115:3. Improvement in weight-related conditions — type 2 diabetes, high blood pressure, sleep apnoea, joint pain. Qualify that outcomes differ between individuals.
content-briefs/gastric-sleeve-perth.md:117:5. Keyhole approach — smaller incisions than open surgery; pain, hospital stay and recovery vary by individual and surgical circumstances.
content-briefs/gastric-sleeve-perth.md:125:  1. Staple line leak — occurs in roughly 1–3% of cases; the most serious early complication, monitored closely and may require further treatment.
content-briefs/gastric-sleeve-perth.md:138:- Medicare item number 31575 may attract a rebate when MBS requirements are met.
content-briefs/gastric-sleeve-perth.md:140:- A cost guide breaks down components and funding options including private health insurance and early-access superannuation for eligible cases.
content-briefs/gastric-sleeve-perth.md:157:5. What does recovery actually look like week to week?
content-briefs/gastric-sleeve-perth.md:165:- **Medical advertising:** No guarantees. Use phrases like "clinical averages", "results vary", "individual results depend on", "your surgeon will advise".
content-briefs/gastric-sleeve-perth.md:166:- **AHPRA/TGA:** No testimonials, no before/after claims, no guaranteed outcomes, no exaggerated claims about effectiveness. GLP-1 / medical-weight-management advertising policy is pending a TGA/legal decision; use only active-ingredient or class names such as semaglutide, liraglutide and GLP-1, with no brand names or comparative claims until confirmed.
content-briefs/gastric-sleeve-perth.md:167:- **Voice:** Plain-language, empathetic, direct. No hype. No "life-changing" or "transformative" without qualification. Write for a real person who is anxious and doing research — not for a brochure.
content-briefs/gastric-sleeve-perth.md:169:- **Surgeon credentials to include:** Dr Harsha Chandraratna (MBBS, FRACS, Bariatric & Upper GI Surgeon; personal bariatric surgery experience; senior lecturer Notre Dame University; operates at SJOG Murdoch and Subiaco) and Dr Stephen Watson (MBBS, FRACS, Bariatric Surgeon; accredited bariatric surgeon at SJOG Murdoch and Subiaco).
docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/gastric-sleeve-perth.md:3:Reason: Safety, Medicare eligibility, hospital verification, cost certainty and outcome-claim issues need correction before publication.
