content-briefs/gastric-bypass-perth.md:86:- **Para 3:** Note that the operation may be performed keyhole (laparoscopic) through small incisions. Wound size, pain, scarring, recovery time and complications vary; the surgeon confirms whether a keyhole approach is appropriate at consultation.
content-briefs/gastric-bypass-perth.md:93:- **BMI note:** Eligibility is assessed individually. For Medicare-funded bariatric surgery, MBS criteria generally describe clinically severe obesity as a BMI of 40 or higher, or a BMI of 35 or higher with a major medical comorbidity. A BMI below those thresholds does not meet these MBS criteria; any other clinical discussion must be confirmed by the surgical team.
