content-reviews/bariatric-surgery-perth.md:5:**Why:** Prescription-medicine references, safety wording, Medicare/private-health certainty, hospital verification and hub-page structure need correction before publication.
content-reviews/bariatric-surgery-perth.md:11:1. **TGA prescription-medicine risk: semaglutide is named in public-facing promotional copy**
content-reviews/bariatric-surgery-perth.md:13:> Medical weight management: non-surgical weight loss treatment pathways including GLP-1 medications (such as semaglutide) and structured dietitian-led programs.
content-reviews/bariatric-surgery-perth.md:17:Why it matters: TGA states that "advertising prescription medicines to the public is prohibited" and specifically calls out weight-loss injections in compliance action, so naming semaglutide on a promotional service page is a publish risk: https://www.tga.gov.au/news/media-releases/tga-releases-new-guidance-advertising-restrictions-prescription-medicines.
