content-reviews/gastric-bypass-perth.md:412:> Keyhole surgery uses small incisions; wound size, pain, scarring, recovery time and complications vary. Your surgeon will confirm whether a keyhole approach is appropriate for you.
content-reviews/gastric-bypass-perth.md:414:Why it matters: The current sentence is close to the brief wording and includes a surgeon-confirms qualifier, but it still risks sounding like a softer pain-and-recovery promise; the writer followed the brief as instructed, so the brief also needs correction.
content-reviews/gastric-bypass-perth.md:444:> Many patients return to light daily activities gradually over the first few weeks, with return to work and heavier activity depending on the type of work, recovery progress and surgeon advice.
content-reviews/gastric-bypass-perth.md:466:> A gastric bypass is one of the most effective bariatric procedures available, but results depend on a combination of surgery and sustained lifestyle change.
content-reviews/gastric-bypass-perth.md:470:Why it matters: "One of the most effective" is a broad claim that does not need to be made for the answer to work.
content-reviews/gastric-bypass-perth.md:488:Summary: The draft has the right broad structure and a useful bypass-vs-sleeve angle, but it is not ready to publish because Medicare/BMI wording, item-number accuracy and risk disclosure need correction.
content-reviews/gastric-bypass-perth.md:490:Summary: Batch-1 additions: G1 added residual claim fixes across the opening, eligibility, benefits, risks, cost and FAQ copy; the GLP-1 scan found 0 references and the pending policy remains flagged. G2 tightened the lower-BMI and condition-based candidate wording. G3 added an exact cut-list, five paste-ready FAQ answers and real destination slugs. G4 flagged 2 scaffolding artifacts for deletion. G5 edited the inherited compliance wording in the brief.
