docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/weight-loss-surgery-perth.md:11:> Medical weight management options including GLP-1s may be suitable if you have a BMI of 30 or higher.
docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/weight-loss-surgery-perth.md:13:> Non-surgical medical weight management may be worth discussing from a BMI of 27 or above, particularly where weight-related health conditions are present. Medication suitability depends on the specific medicine, your medical history and current Australian prescribing guidance, while surgical Medicare eligibility is assessed separately.
docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/weight-loss-surgery-perth.md:15:Why it matters: The specific BMI 30+ suitability claim is too direct and should be framed as an assessment conversation, especially where medication suitability and surgical Medicare eligibility are different questions.
