docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/weight-loss-surgery-perth.md:103:5. **The lower-BMI eligibility bullets are not MBS-accurate** (G2; draft L80-90, including the known residual at draft L88)
docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/weight-loss-surgery-perth.md:105:   > BMI 40+: surgery is generally an appropriate option to discuss, regardless of other conditions
docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/weight-loss-surgery-perth.md:107:   > BMI 35–40 and a related condition such as type 2 diabetes, high blood pressure, sleep apnoea, joint disease, or gastro-oesophageal reflux disease (GORD): surgery is commonly considered
docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/weight-loss-surgery-perth.md:109:   > BMI 30–35: may be considered in select cases, often where diabetes is difficult to manage with medication alone; assessed on an individual basis
docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/weight-loss-surgery-perth.md:111:   > Eligibility is assessed individually. For a Medicare-listed bariatric surgery pathway, the relevant MBS thresholds are BMI 40+ or BMI 35+ with a major co-morbidity; a BMI below 35 does not meet that MBS threshold. Your surgeon must assess the clinical options, risks and suitability for your circumstances.
docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/weight-loss-surgery-perth.md:113:   This replaces the implication that BMI 30-35 is a surgical pathway and avoids treating “may be considered” as eligibility.
docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/weight-loss-surgery-perth.md:123:   > A commonly used 30/30 approach is to avoid drinking for about 30 minutes before a meal and wait about 30 minutes after eating before drinking again. Your dietitian or surgeon will confirm whether this applies at your stage of recovery and give you the relevant eating and drinking plan.
docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/weight-loss-surgery-perth.md:126:   > The MBS thresholds are BMI 40+ or BMI 35+ with a major co-morbidity. A person below BMI 35 does not meet that MBS threshold; a person at BMI 35-39.9 needs the relevant major co-morbidity. Clinical suitability also depends on medical history, surgical risk, readiness for follow-up and individual clinician assessment.
docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/weight-loss-surgery-perth.md:129:   > Medicare may provide rebates for eligible specialist consultations and MBS-listed bariatric surgery services when current criteria are met. The relevant procedure items are 31575 for sleeve gastrectomy, 31572 for Roux-en-Y gastric bypass and 31581 for BPD/duodenal switch. Private health cover, waiting periods, hospital excess and anaesthetist fees can affect out-of-pocket costs, so confirm what applies before deciding.
docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/weight-loss-surgery-perth.md:170:> Obesity Surgery WA brings together surgeons, physicians, Accredited Practising Dietitians and exercise physiologists, with 20+ years supporting weight loss in Perth, clinics in Booragoon and Mandurah, and individual medical assessment available for some people at BMI 27+ where clinically appropriate.
docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/weight-loss-surgery-perth.md:176:> You may be eligible for weight loss surgery if you have a BMI of 40 or higher, or 35 or higher with a weight-related health condition such as type 2 diabetes or high blood pressure, and where diet and exercise alone have not produced long-term results.
docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/weight-loss-surgery-perth.md:178:> A BMI of 27 or above, particularly where a weight-related health condition is present, is a reason to request an individual medical assessment for non-surgical options. Surgical Medicare eligibility must be assessed separately; current MBS criteria refer to BMI 40+ or BMI 35+ with a major co-morbidity, with suitability assessed by your surgeon.
docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/weight-loss-surgery-perth.md:186:> Is weight loss surgery covered by Medicare in Australia? Medicare may provide rebates for eligible specialist consultations and MBS-listed bariatric surgery services when current criteria are met. The relevant procedure items are 31575 for sleeve gastrectomy, 31572 for Roux-en-Y gastric bypass and 31581 for BPD/duodenal switch. Private health cover, waiting periods, hospital excess and anaesthetist fees can affect out-of-pocket costs, so confirm what applies before deciding.
docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/weight-loss-surgery-perth.md:198:7. **The draft is roughly 50% over the 1,100-1,400 word target**
docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/weight-loss-surgery-perth.md:241:> We have consulting rooms in Booragoon and Greenfields, keeping appointments accessible for patients across Perth and the south-west. Surgeries are performed at [<u>Mount Private Hospital</u>](https://mountprivatehospital.com.au), [<u>The Park Private Hospital</u>](https://www.tpph.com.au/), and [<u>Waikiki Private Hospital</u>](https://waikikiprivate.com.au/). Once your surgery is planned, our team will walk you through exactly what to expect, where to go, and who will be involved at every stage, so there are no surprises on the day.
docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/weight-loss-surgery-perth.md:243:> We have consulting rooms in Booragoon and Mandurah, keeping appointments accessible for patients across Perth and the south-west. Surgeries are performed at [hospital identity to be verified]. Once your surgery is planned, our team will walk you through exactly what to expect, where to go, and who will be involved at every stage.
docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/weight-loss-surgery-perth.md:249:> Surgery is not the only pathway forward. Because obesity is a medical condition — not a willpower failure — the right treatment looks different for every person. Options range from GLP-1 medications and structured very low calorie diets, to dietitian-led nutrition support, exercise guidance, endoscopic procedures, and surgery.
docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/weight-loss-surgery-perth.md:263:Why it matters: The existing qualifier helps, but the sentence still needs softer outcome language and clearer individual-variation framing.
docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/weight-loss-surgery-perth.md:277:> From GLP-1 medications and structured diet programs through to sleeve, bypass, and band procedures, the weight loss treatment spectrum is broader than most people realise.
docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/weight-loss-surgery-perth.md:292:Summary: Main fixes are to separate surgical eligibility from medical management, add direct Medicare/minimum-BMI/cost FAQs, and cut 500+ words.
docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/weight-loss-surgery-perth.md:297:- **Hospitals:** Use the canonical paste-ready surgery-location replacement in Should fix 8b above. The hospital identity remains unverified until the client confirms the correct facilities; do not choose one side in the copy.
docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/weight-loss-surgery-perth.md:298:- **GLP-1 policy:** The TGA/legal advertising decision for GLP-1 and medical-weight-management copy is pending. Keep active-ingredient/class references only (semaglutide, liraglutide or GLP-1), never brands, and verify the final policy before publication.
