docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/gastric-bypass-perth.md:432:> The Obesity Surgery WA surgical team performs gastric bypass surgery in Perth at three locations: [<u>Mount Private Hospital</u>](https://mountprivatehospital.com.au), [<u>The Park Private Hospital</u>](https://www.tpph.com.au/), and [<u>Waikiki Private Hospital</u>](https://waikikiprivate.com.au/). Pre- and post-operative (once you’ve been discharged from hospital) consultations take place at Garden City Specialist Centre, Booragoon, and WA Cardiology Centre in Greenfields.
docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/gastric-bypass-perth.md:436:Why it matters: Q1 remains open. Verify the hospital identity with the client before replacing the draft list; the neutral replacement keeps the page publishable without choosing between conflicting sources.
docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/gastric-bypass-perth.md:438:23. **Add a "who is not eligible" FAQ**
docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/gastric-bypass-perth.md:444:> **Who is not eligible for gastric bypass?** For Medicare-funded bariatric surgery, a BMI below 40 without a major medical comorbidity, or a BMI below 35, does not meet the stated MBS eligibility threshold. Surgery may also be unsuitable if health risks, anatomy or the ability to follow long-term nutrition and follow-up need further assessment. Eligibility and alternatives must be discussed with your surgeon.
docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/gastric-bypass-perth.md:446:Why it matters: The page should answer the negative eligibility question without implying that a condition, BMI or online checklist guarantees access to surgery.
docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/gastric-bypass-perth.md:460:1. **The keyhole-surgery sentence should be more qualified [also fix the brief]**
docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/gastric-bypass-perth.md:462:> The small keyhole incisions mean less pain post-operatively, smaller scars, and generally, a faster recovery than open surgery, though your surgeon will discuss your goals and your different surgical options during your initial consultation.
docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/gastric-bypass-perth.md:464:> Keyhole surgery uses small incisions; wound size, pain, scarring, recovery time and complications vary. Your surgeon will confirm whether a keyhole approach is appropriate for you.
docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/gastric-bypass-perth.md:466:Why it matters: The current sentence is close to the brief wording and includes a surgeon-confirms qualifier, but it still risks sounding like a softer pain-and-recovery promise; the writer followed the brief as instructed, so the brief also needs correction.
docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/gastric-bypass-perth.md:496:> Many patients return to light daily activities gradually over the first few weeks, with return to work and heavier activity depending on the type of work, recovery progress and surgeon advice.
docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/gastric-bypass-perth.md:520:> A gastric bypass is one of the most effective bariatric procedures available, but results depend on a combination of surgery and sustained lifestyle change.
docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/gastric-bypass-perth.md:524:Why it matters: "One of the most effective" is a broad claim that does not need to be made for the answer to work.
docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/gastric-bypass-perth.md:544:Summary: The draft has the right broad structure and a useful bypass-vs-sleeve angle, but it is not ready to publish because Medicare/BMI wording, item-number accuracy and risk disclosure need correction.
docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/gastric-bypass-perth.md:546:Summary: Batch-1 additions: G1 added 14 residual quote/replacement fixes across extracted L47-L69, L112-L117, L175-L193, L208-L210, L251-L255, L259-L266, L291-L297, L302-L308, L312-L317 and L321-L328; the GLP-1 scan found 0 references and the pending policy remains flagged. G2 tightened the lower-BMI and condition-based candidate wording at extracted L101-L104 and L112-L117, with the brief corrected at L93-L96. G3 added an exact cut-list, five paste-ready FAQ answers and real destination slugs. G4 flagged 2 scaffolding artifacts for deletion at extracted L238-L244. G5 edited the inherited compliance wording in the brief.
docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/bariatric-surgery-perth.md:3:Reason: Prescription-medicine references, safety wording, Medicare/private-health certainty, hospital verification and hub-page structure need correction before publication.
docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/bariatric-surgery-perth.md:9:1. **TGA prescription-medicine risk: semaglutide is named in public-facing promotional copy**
docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/bariatric-surgery-perth.md:11:> Medical weight management: non-surgical weight loss treatment pathways including GLP-1 medications (such as semaglutide) and structured dietitian-led programs.
docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/bariatric-surgery-perth.md:15:Why it matters: TGA states that "advertising prescription medicines to the public is prohibited" and specifically calls out weight-loss injections in compliance action, so naming semaglutide on a promotional service page is a publish risk: https://www.tga.gov.au/news/media-releases/tga-releases-new-guidance-advertising-restrictions-prescription-medicines.
docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/bariatric-surgery-perth.md:17:2. **The FAQ promotes GLP-1 treatment without enough balance [also fix the brief]**
docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/bariatric-surgery-perth.md:19:> Medical weight management, including GLP-1 medications and dietitian-led programs, is a genuine and effective option for many people, and our team offers this alongside surgical pathways.
docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/bariatric-surgery-perth.md:25:3. **The risks section uses an unbalanced "safe" claim [also fix the brief]**
docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/bariatric-surgery-perth.md:27:> Every surgical procedure carries risk, though modern keyhole techniques and highly experienced surgeons make bariatric procedures safe for most suitable candidates.
docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/bariatric-surgery-perth.md:41:5. **The opening section keeps a GLP-1 class reference [also fix the brief]**
