   386	  >
   387	  > **7. I have had weight loss surgery before — can it be revised?** Yes, revision surgery is available for patients whose previous procedure is no longer working as intended, has caused complications, or requires conversion to a different procedure. Common examples include removing or converting an older gastric band, or converting a sleeve to a bypass. Revision surgery is generally more complex than a primary procedure, and your surgeon will assess your history carefully before making any recommendation.
