   330	>
   331	> **9. Does Medicare cover weight loss surgery?** Medicare benefits may apply when the relevant MBS item, clinical and referral requirements are met, but Medicare does not cover every cost and no rebate should be assumed. The applicable item depends on the procedure—31575 is sleeve gastrectomy, 31572 is Roux-en-Y gastric bypass and 31581 is BPD/duodenal switch—so your surgeon and insurer should confirm what applies.
   332	>
   333	> **10. What is the 30/30 eating rule after bariatric surgery?** Many bariatric programs use a 30/30 approach: take about 30 minutes to eat and separate drinks from meals by about 30 minutes. It is a general postoperative guide, not a universal rule; your surgeon or dietitian will tailor advice to your procedure and stage of recovery.
